{
 "sections": [
  {
   "title": "Act 7: Two Wars and a General",
   "beats": [
    {
     "id": "s08b01",
     "shot": "ww1",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "World War One took around 1.4 million French soldiers.",
     "date": 1918,
     "sfx": [],
     "quiet": true
    },
    {
     "id": "s08b02",
     "shot": "ww1",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "By some counts, more than a quarter of French men aged 18 to 27 were killed.",
     "date": 1918,
     "sfx": [],
     "quiet": true
    },
    {
     "id": "s08b03",
     "shot": "fall1940",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "Then in 1940 Germany conquered France in about six weeks.",
     "date": 1940,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "rumble",
       8,
       0.5
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s08b04",
     "shot": "vichy",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "A marshal signed an armistice, a collaborating government set up in the spa town",
     "date": 1940,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "paper",
       "w:armistice,",
       0.4
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s08b05",
     "shot": "vichy",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "of Vichy, and a general nobody had heard of,",
     "date": 1940,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "pop2",
       "w:general",
       0.4
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s08b06",
     "shot": "radio",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "Charles de Gaulle, spoke on the radio from London on 18 June and told",
     "date": 1940,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "blip",
       6,
       0.3
      ]
     ],
     "mood": "grand"
    },
    {
     "id": "s08b07",
     "shot": "radio",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "the French that France had lost a battle, not the war.",
     "date": 1940,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "blip",
       6,
       0.3
      ]
     ],
     "mood": "grand"
    },
    {
     "id": "s08b08",
     "shot": "liberation",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "After liberation in 1944, France tried again.",
     "date": 1944,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "pops",
       10,
       0.3
      ]
     ],
     "mood": "grand"
    },
    {
     "id": "s08b09",
     "shot": "revolving_door",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "The Fourth Republic, born in 1946, put parliament in charge and kept the president weak.",
     "date": 1946,
     "sfx": []
    },
    {
     "id": "s08b10",
     "shot": "revolving_door",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "It went through more than twenty governments in twelve years.",
     "date": 1958,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "whoosh",
       4,
       0.3
      ],
      [
       "ticks",
       "w:twenty",
       0.4
      ]
     ],
     "mood": "playful"
    },
    {
     "id": "s08b11",
     "shot": "algeria58",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "When a crisis over Algeria in 1958 pushed the army toward revolt,",
     "date": 1958,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "drum",
       4,
       0.4
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s08b12",
     "shot": "algeria58",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "parliament turned to the one man everybody trusted.",
     "date": 1958,
     "sfx": []
    },
    {
     "id": "s08b13",
     "shot": "fifth_republic",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "De Gaulle rewrote the constitution.",
